{"commit": "2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292", "id": "2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: ", "repo": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/aho-corasick", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T153450Z-cb4da37c", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1/20260923T153450Z-cb4da37c/origin.json": "ba41b10580bf438b2969e113850cad05b5bce256f01574c670e38eb24dda5d32", "evidence/2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1/20260923T153450Z-cb4da37c/proposal.json": "6c9918dd6fac00af1daf9d627612a2babe8d757d8231adb195532d1ec06e09c3"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "aho-corasick", "status": "blocked", "subject": "prefilter: fix a prefilter bug", "summary": "A pattern-ID desync between the Aho-Corasick NFA and the packed prefilter. In leftmost-first mode, a pattern whose prefix is already accepted short-circuits NFA compilation, so the prefilter's pattern-ID counter fell behind and later patterns ended up with the wrong IDs \u2014 producing mismatched `find_iter` output depending on whether the prefilter was enabled.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T15:34:50.974271+00:00"}
{"commit": "2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292", "id": "2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: ", "repo": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/aho-corasick", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T153458Z-6d108d74", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1/20260923T153458Z-6d108d74/origin.json": "6bf1938037b6f3f3af71cf7b9b8861d5f57dd6c31fde57432aa4086f148e96e3", "evidence/2df0983e7ef76bf50e6213fee35cda87af191292-1/20260923T153458Z-6d108d74/proposal.json": "328989839a40e21b2024c4ab23d41b71ae2afafb2670b4b146bb50a02814c5e5"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "aho-corasick", "status": "blocked", "subject": "prefilter: fix a prefilter bug", "summary": "A pattern-ID desync between the Aho-Corasick NFA and the packed prefilter. In leftmost-first mode, a pattern whose prefix is already accepted short-circuits NFA compilation, so the prefilter's pattern-ID counter fell behind and later patterns ended up with the wrong IDs \u2014 producing mismatched `find_iter` output depending on whether the prefilter was enabled.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T15:34:58.765526+00:00"}
